{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"Whether the migrated session was found and opened. False means the open fell back to the legacy session the host had just migrated away from.","endPoint":"none","isMeasurement":true,"purpose":"FeatureInsight"}},"agentHost.legacyCopilotCliMigrationProbe":{"comment":"Counts adopt-on-open probe attempts for legacy extension-host Copilot CLI sessions. The host-side agentHost.legacyCopilotCliMigration event only fires once migration starts, so without this there is no denominator for a success rate and a silently-unmigrated open is indistinguishable from a user having no legacy sessions.","durationms":{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"Time in milliseconds spent probing before the outcome was known.","endPoint":"none","isMeasurement":true,"purpose":"PerformanceAndHealth"},"outcome":{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"Probe outcome: adopted (the host migrated the session; the caller may still fall back if it does not surface — see agentHost.legacyCopilotCliMigrationOpen), declined (host refused, e.g. not an adoptable legacy chat), timedOut (no answer within the budget), settingDisabled, noConnection, or failed (probe threw).","endPoint":"none","purpose":"FeatureInsight"},"owner":"vijayupadya","source":{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"Entry point that probed: open (user opened a session) or restore (startup/editor restore).","endPoint":"none","purpose":"FeatureInsight"},"timeoutms":{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"The probe budget that applied, so timeouts can be correlated with the entry point.","endPoint":"none","isMeasurement":true,"purpose":"PerformanceAndHealth"}},"agentHost.modelCallTurnCorrelated":{"comment":"Records exact model-call ownership independently of response telemetry arrival. Deduplicated by SDK session and call ID; the first owner is retained and a later conflicting owner is emitted with mappingStatus conflict so consumers can exclude it, not dropped here.","mappingstatus":{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"Whether ownership was recorded, arrived after forwarding, or conflicts with an owner retained in the bounded cache.","endPoint":"none","purpose":"PerformanceAndHealth"},"modelcallid":{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"Call identifier from model completion; join only by exact ID, never by time. Message fallback IDs may have no corresponding SDK response.","endPoint":"none","purpose":"PerformanceAndHealth"},"owner":"amunger","sdksessionid":{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"SDK session ID matching sdk_session_id on forwarded response events.","endPoint":"none","purpose":"PerformanceAndHealth"},"turnid":{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"Host-remapped turn owning the completed model call.","endPoint":"none","purpose":"PerformanceAndHealth"}},"agentHost.processError":{"callstack":{"classification":"CallstackOrException","comment":"The callstack of an agent host process start failure.","endPoint":"none","purpose":"PerformanceAndHealth"},"code":{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"The agent host process exit code, when available.","endPoint":"none","isMeasurement":true,"purpose":"PerformanceAndHealth"},"comment":"Tracks agent host process failures that cannot be reported reliably from inside the agent host process.","hostlaunchkind":{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"Whether the agent host process was launched by the VS Code main process or VS Code CLI.","endPoint":"none","purpose":"PerformanceAndHealth"},"iserror":{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"Whether this is an error event.","endPoint":"none","isMeasurement":true,"purpose":"PerformanceAndHealth"},"kind":{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"The kind of agent host process failure.","endPoint":"none","purpose":"PerformanceAndHealth"},"msg":{"classification":"CallstackOrException","comment":"The message of an agent host process start failure.","endPoint":"none","purpose":"PerformanceAndHealth"},"owner":"bryanchen-d","restartcount":{"classification":"SystemMetaData","comment":"The number of agent host restart attempts before